            <h3 id="sec4-2"><span class="sec-num">4.2</span> Counterfactual Falsification Matrix (CF-1 through CF-4)</h3>
            <p>To prove strict causality rather than coincidence, we deliberately broke each theorem&rsquo;s governing mechanism on live T4&times;2 hardware (Figure 2):</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>CF-1 (Break Theorem 1):</strong> With <code>.detach()</code> on <code>CG-LatFiLM</code>, gradient leakage from Stream 0&rsquo;s loss into Stream 1&rsquo;s weights is exact <code>0.00000000</code>. Removing <code>.detach()</code> immediately causes non-zero gradient leakage (2.02 &times; 10<sup>&minus;9</sup> &gt; 0).</li>
              <li><strong>CF-2 (Break Theorem 2A):</strong> Removing <code>.detach()</code> at block boundaries on <em>K</em> = 4 causes peak activation VRAM to rebound <strong>3.45&times;</strong> (219.6 &rarr; 758.1 MB, returning identically to <em>K</em> = 1 Global BP).</li>
              <li><strong>CF-3 (Break Theorem 3 on T4&times;2):</strong> Re-introducing synchronous backward-locked pipeline bubbles degrades 2-GPU latency from <strong>16.96 ms</strong> to <strong>41.82 ms</strong> (confirming a <strong>2.47&times;</strong> real 2-GPU speedup on identical parameters).</li>
              <li><strong>CF-4 (Break Anti-Myopia):</strong> Removing Deep-MAN++ EMA shadows drops <code>AffCIFAR-10</code> Pose <em>R</em><sup>2</sup> (+0.325 &rarr; +0.308) and class accuracy (77.58% &rarr; 77.08%).</li>
            </ul>

